#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""craftov: run the Craftov test server on this Mac for the agent on the dev server.

A remote-gate extension (see mac-bridge): installed as
~/.local/libexec/remote-gate/craftov, it answers `ssh mac craftov ...`. Every
command works on one checkout only, ~/Documents/projects/plugins/EscapeFromCraftov
(or the path written in ~/.config/craftov-gate/project).

  craftov status                 checkout, server state and connection settings
  craftov head                   the checked-out commit and branch
  craftov branches               local branches and recent commits
  craftov bundle                 a git bundle of every local branch, on stdout
  craftov sync [--park <name>]   fast-forward the checkout to `main` from a git
                                 bundle on stdin (git bundle create - main);
                                 --park renames a branch with commits the
                                 bundle lacks to <name> instead of refusing.
                                 Then installs the checkout's tools/mac/craftov
                                 over this extension if it differs
  craftov selfupdate             install a new version of this extension read
                                 from stdin
  craftov jar                    install a plugin jar read from stdin as
                                 server/run/plugins/Craftov.jar
  craftov build                  ./gradlew deployLocal here, with JDK 25
  craftov setup                  create server/run with server/setup.sh --local
  craftov start | stop | restart run the server in the background; start and
                                 restart wait for "Done"
  craftov rcon <command...>      run a console command over RCON
  craftov log [lines]            the end of server/run/logs/latest.log
  craftov consolelog [lines]     the end of server/run/console.log (the server's
                                 stdout, with errors from before Paper's log opens)
  craftov clientlog [lines]      the end of the Minecraft client log
  craftov yml diff <file>        compare plugins/Craftov/<file> with the repo copy
  craftov yml copy <file>        replace it with the repo copy (keeps a backup);
                                 <file> is items.yml or loot.yml (diff: config.yml too)
  craftov packip <IPv4>          the address CraftEngine advertises the pack at

sync, jar and build run code from the repository on this Mac: that is the
point of the extension, and why it touches nothing outside the checkout and
itself. Updating itself adds nothing to that: a plugin the server sends can
already rewrite this file.
"""
